        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@majjoha, I understand that this was a very long delay and it might be irrelevant, but your request is now possible with [config.custom_surroundings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/297993c40e93bd155d72424e3a1abeefb3be344e/doc/mini.txt#L3784) option. Your use case is (almost fully) possible with the following setup:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    ['('] = { output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' } },\r\n    ['['] = { output = { left = '[ ', right = ' ]' } },\r\n    ['{'] = { output = { left = '{ ', right = ' }' } },\r\n    ['<'] = { output = { left = '< ', right = ' >' } },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis will add (like in `saiw(` or `sr\"(`) parentheses/brackets with spaces but will find and delete (like in `sd(`) without spaces. The latter is, unfortunately, not possible under current design and, probably, won't be.",
            "created_at": "2022-04-19T17:16:28Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/16#issuecomment-1102896229",
            "id": 1102896229,
